From: Jianping Li <jianping.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250, sm8750: make the ADSP remote heap no-map

The two patches of "arm64: dts: qcom: Make ADSP remote heaps no-map" that reach
our SoCs, in upstream order:

 3/4 arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: Make the ADSP remote heap no-map
     <20261015071511.977-4-jianping.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
 4/4 arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: Make the ADSP remote heap no-map
     <20261015071511.977-5-jianping.li@oss.qualcomm.com>

The ADSP remote heap is declared as a reusable shared DMA pool. FastRPC assigns
the entire region to the DSP during probe without allocating the pages from
CMA, so movable HLOS allocations can land on pages HLOS no longer has access
to, and the kernel then takes synchronous external aborts on them.

Replace reusable with no-map to keep the region reserved for the DSP and out of
the kernel's standard memory mapping.

Fixes: 531ce288b6dd4 ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: Add memory-region for audio PD")
Fixes: 0bcf9ca23a873 ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add memory node for adsp fastrpc")
Signed-off-by: Jianping Li <jianping.li@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Ekansh Gupta <ekansh.gupta@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
index ccb940275..3f32c5082 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -868,7 +868,7 @@ cdsp_secure_heap: memory@8bf00000 {
 		adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
-			reusable;
+			no-map;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			size = <0x0 0x800000>;
 		};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index c203f7ce8..e3acfa4f5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -570,7 +570,7 @@ adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
 			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			size = <0x0 0xc00000>;
-			reusable;
+			no-map;
 		};
 	};
 
